id: pm-3zh9s4
title: "MCP remote authorization and observability: issuer-bound credentials, client metadata documents, consent, header security, and OpenTelemetry propagation"
description: "Define and implement the 2026-07-28 remote MCP trust boundary for Streamable HTTP, including authorization discovery, issuer validation, registration migration, consent, trace context, and abuse resistance."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[8]: "area:mcp",authorization,client-metadata,issuer,oauth,opentelemetry,privacy,security
created_at: "2026-08-25T05:10:30.953Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-25T23:00:44.967Z"
deadline: "2026-11-30T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-25T23:00:44.318Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-25T23:00:44.318Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 960
acceptance_criteria: "Authorization-server discovery and issuer pinning prevent credentials from being reused or redeemed at a different issuer; Present iss values are validated and dynamic registration fallback is bounded behind Client ID Metadata Document preference; application_type, redirect URI, scopes, consent, refresh, revocation, and re-registration behavior have positive and negative tests; Header mappings, proxies, caches, traces, logs, errors, and telemetry cannot leak tokens, secrets, workspace paths, or private resource content; traceparent, tracestate, and baggage propagation follows explicit allowlists, byte limits, and redaction; A threat model and real Streamable HTTP integration suite gate release"
goal: Secure observable remote pm MCP
objective: "Make every remote request attributable, authorized, consented, privacy-bounded, and traceable without credential or context leakage"
value: "Organizations can expose pm remotely without unsafe token reuse, redirect ambiguity, header injection, or opaque failures"
why_now: "The revision tightens issuer and application-type validation, binds credentials to authorization servers, prefers Client ID Metadata Documents, and defines trace-context propagation"
parent: pm-rs9vry
risk: critical
confidence: medium
resolution: Implemented and verified
expected_result: "Issuer-bound, scope-bounded remote MCP authorization and privacy-safe trace propagation."
actual_result: "RFC 9728 discovery, issuer/PKCE/registration controls, credential lifecycle, bearer enforcement, trace limits, docs, and adversarial tests all pass."
