comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T05:10:30.953Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for MCP authorization iss issuer binding application_type client ID metadata documents dynamic registration consent headers and OpenTelemetry. No current item owns the remote 2026-07-28 trust boundary."
  "2026-08-25T19:16:15.394Z","harness:codex","Execution scope: issuer-bound authorization helpers, Client ID Metadata Document preference, protected-resource and scope validation, safe transport headers, OpenTelemetry context allowlists/redaction, threat-model docs, and adversarial tests."
  "2026-08-25T19:54:42.079Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: added RFC 9728 metadata, exact issuer discovery and response validation, S256 enforcement, Client ID Metadata Document preference with bounded DCR fallback, issuer-keyed credential replacement/revocation primitives, issuer/audience/scope bearer enforcement, constant-time opaque token verification, and W3C trace/baggage isolation. Unit adversarial and real HTTP authorization suites are green; the deployment threat model documents host-owned refresh and revocation boundaries."
  "2026-08-25T21:13:13.034Z","harness:codex","Evidence: shipped RFC 9728 protected-resource metadata, issuer/S256 and registration policy validation, CIMD/DCR helpers, permission-bounded credential storage, bearer scope enforcement, trace/baggage propagation, and secure remote-server environment defaults. Exact repository verification passed 581 files / 7,982 tests at 100/100/100/100; focused authorization and Streamable HTTP tests passed; pnpm quality:static, pnpm lint, pnpm typecheck, SDK surface verification, package artifact validation, npx smoke, and package-first dogfood all passed."
  "2026-08-25T21:46:20.022Z","harness:codex","Review evidence: pre-PR concurrency analysis found that HTTP clients can reuse client-local JSON-RPC ids and that a disconnected sink must not fail an unrelated mutation. The transport wrapper now scopes each HTTP stream with an opaque key, broadcasts through isolated registries, prunes failed sinks, and closes stdio-only streams independently. Negative controls cover duplicate IDs, stale-sink isolation, and mixed stdio/HTTP shutdown; the final exact run passed 581 files / 7,986 tests at 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-25T22:57:39.407Z","harness:codex","Hosted-review remediation evidence (final code before close): authorization metadata validation now requires authorization_endpoint and token_endpoint at runtime; bearer authentication is case-insensitive; malformed non-string method values fail closed; discovery issuer path joining strips boundary slashes while credential-store issuer identity remains exact by design because MCP/OAuth issuer matching uses simple string comparison and path trailing slashes may be semantically distinct. Added minimal-metadata, malformed-method, bearer-case, path-distinction, and branch coverage. Exact local proof: 581 files / 7,990 tests at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines; full lint/static chain exited 0."
  "2026-08-25T23:00:41.606Z","harness:codex","Final linked-test execution after hosted-review remediation: the authorization/transport/HTTP suite passed 27/27 tests with no skips."
